      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $(Q⇒P)⇒R.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Q⇒P)⇒R & ≡(¬Q∨P)⇒R \\\\  & ≡¬(¬Q∨P)∨R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬Q∨P)∨R≡(¬(¬Q)∧¬P)∨R\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n(¬(¬Q)∧¬P)∨R≡(Q∧¬P)∨R.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $(Q∧¬P)∨R.$",
